<title>INDIA: Indian soybean ends up on demand from processors.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean ends up on demand from processors.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian soybean prices ended Wednesday firm on strong demand, traders said.</p>
<p>They said prices were up 50-100 rupees per tonne on good demand from processors in active trade. The undertone was firm, they said.</p>
<p>Soyoil refined was down 300 rupees per tonne on selling from plants and refineries but soyoil solvent was steady, traders said.</p>
<p>They said soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices were firm on good export enquiry.</p>
<p>Soymeal yellow was $258-260 per tonne FAS (Free alongside ship) west coast Indian ports for export.</p>
<p>Rapeseed extraction was $99-100 FAS (Free alongside ship) in bulk for export and 3,275-3,300 rupees per tonne in FOR (Free on rail) condition. The undertone was firm, traders said.</p>
